  "$comment": "Steam Controller 2 byte bookkeeping, hand-written. out_report_len: each output report's wire length with the id byte (pf_driver_proto::triton::out_report_len; the Apple and Android strippedOutputLen is one less), null = undeclared, sent whole. imu_trace: reports fed in order through one fresh IMU gate (punktfunk-core client::sc2, which gates every client's raw reports); the report carries ts as a little-endian u32 at byte 30 with non-zero IMU bytes after it, and pass means the IMU bytes leave unchanged, else they are zeroed. buttons: a state-report button bit (sc2, SDL TritonButtons) and the punktfunk wire bit it means (punktfunk_core::input gamepad BTN_*); the host fallback (triton_proto::from_gamepad), Swift wireMap and Kotlin WIRE_MAP replay it. 0x40 is Start (menu) and 0x4000 is Select (view), as SDL's mapping and hid-steam have them; SDL's enum names are the other way round.",
